  "role": "American football quarterback (NFL 2011–2016) and civil-rights activist",
  "summary": "Kaepernick became a prominent activist after kneeling during the national anthem in 2016 to protest police brutality and racial inequality. He has since advocated the abolition of police and prisons, founded the Know Your Rights Camp, and supported Indigenous causes. He declined to vote in 2016, calling it support for a system of oppression, but later voted in 2020 and 2024 and in his 2026 memoir called that earlier choice irresponsible.",
